    "outcome": "Lenz's law: direction of the induced current and force",
    "stem": {
     "type": "doc",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "marks": [],
         "type": "text",
         "text": "A rectangular conducting loop lies in the plane of the page. Part of the loop is in a region of uniform magnetic field that is directed "
        },
        {
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "bold"
          }
         ],
         "type": "text",
         "text": "into"
        },
        {
         "marks": [],
         "type": "text",
         "text": " the page. The loop is pulled to the right, out of the field region, at constant speed."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "figure",
       "attrs": {
        "stimulus_id": "fig1"
       }
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "marks": [],
         "type": "text",
         "text": "Which describes the direction of the induced current in the loop, as seen by an observer looking at the page, and the direction of the magnetic force on the loop?"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    "stimuli": [
     {
      "id": "fig1",
      "kind": "schematic_diagram",
      "use": "read_only",
      "description": "A rectangular conducting frame in the plane of the page. On the left, a region of uniform magnetic field into the page (⊗ symbols) ends at a vertical boundary line; there is no field to the right of the boundary. The left side of the frame is inside the field and the right side is outside. A velocity arrow (v) pointing right is drawn on the frame. Current directions are defined as seen by an observer looking at the page. Diagram not to scale.",
      "asset_id": null,
      "alt_text": null
     }
    ],
    "mcq": {
     "option_kind": "statement",
     "option_layout": "single_value",
     "column_headers": [],
     "statements": [],
     "options": [
      {
       "key": "A",
       "cells": [
        {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "content": [
            {
             "marks": [],
             "type": "text",
             "text": "The current is clockwise and the force is to the left."
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ],
       "rationale": null
      },
      {
       "key": "B",
       "cells": [
        {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "content": [
            {
             "marks": [],
             "type": "text",
             "text": "The current is clockwise and the force is to the right."
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ],
       "rationale": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "marks": [],
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Current direction correct; but thinks the force assists the motion (contradicts conservation of energy) or applies the hand rule the wrong way round"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "key": "C",
       "cells": [
        {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "content": [
            {
             "marks": [],
             "type": "text",
             "text": "The current is anticlockwise and the force is to the left."
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ],
       "rationale": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "marks": [],
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thinks the induced field is always opposite to the external field (misses that the flux is decreasing); correctly remembers \"opposes the motion\" for the force"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "key": "D",
       "cells": [
        {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "content": [
            {
             "marks": [],
             "type": "text",
             "text": "The current is anticlockwise and the force is to the right."
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ],
       "rationale": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "marks": [],
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thinks the induced field is opposite to the external field, and then finds the force by applying the rule to this current: an anticlockwise current is downwards in the left side, (−y) × (−z) = +x, to the right"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      }
     ],
     "correct_key": "A",
     "explanation": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [],
          "type": "text",
          "text": "As the frame leaves the field, the flux into the page decreases. Lenz's law: the induced current opposes this decrease, that is, it produces a field into the page inside the frame. Right-hand grip rule (fingers curl in the direction of the current, the thumb points along the field inside the loop): for a field into the page the current is clockwise. Force: the clockwise current is towards the top of the page (+y) in the left side, which is in the field. F = IL × B = (+y) × (−z) = −x: to the left. The forces on the parts of the top and bottom sides that are in the field are equal and opposite. The force opposes the motion; consistent with conservation of energy."
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     "assessment_objective": 2,
     "level_content": "ahl",
     "solution_step": null
    },
    "parts": [],
    "total_marks": 1,
    "solution_model": null
   }
